Let a driver seed a new provider's attribute mapping. A provider created through the control panel started with an empty mapping, so a site that did nothing about it synced no claim onto the Plone user at all — the login worked and the account stayed nameless. Drivers now declare a `default_propertymap`, served through `@identity-drivers` and written into the add form, which an operator edits or empties like anything else on it.

It is written against the normalized claim names rather than any one provider's, so `fullname` covers GitHub's `login` fallback and an OIDC `preferred_username` alike without either being named. Only the two fields `IUserDataSchema` declares are mapped: a stock site has no `username` member field, and a default naming one would look right in the form and resolve to nothing on every login. The magic-link driver seeds the address only, a mailbox asserting nothing else. @ericof
